From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:47:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: retry channel equalisation before lowering the
 link rate

When the second training phase (channel equalisation) fails,
msm_dp_ctrl_on_link() immediately lowers the link rate or the lane
count. After a Type-C plug, the first training through a repeater can
fail channel equalisation and then pass with the same parameters on the
next attempt, so the link ends up at a lower rate or lane count than it
can carry.

For external DisplayPort, retry training twice with unchanged
parameters before lowering them. These retries come on top of the
existing attempts, so as many rate and lane count steps remain as
before. eDP panels keep the existing fallback.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index 8e984c62027..bec30315996 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2365,6 +2365,14 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl,
 	struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl;
 	u32 rate;
 	int link_train_max_retries = 5;
+	/*
+	 * Retries with unchanged link parameters before the rate or lane count
+	 * is reduced: the first training after a Type-C plug can fail channel
+	 * equalization at a repeater and pass unchanged on the next attempt.
+	 */
+	int same_params_retries = 2;
+	bool is_edp = panel->connector &&
+		      panel->connector->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP;
 	u32 const phy_cts_pixel_clk_khz = 148500;
 	u8 link_status[DP_LINK_STATUS_SIZE];
 	unsigned int training_step;
@@ -2437,17 +2445,26 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl,
 			if (!msm_dp_aux_link_plugged(ctrl->aux))
 				break;
 
-			drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status(ctrl->aux, link_status);
+			if (!is_edp && same_params_retries-- > 0) {
+				/* Retries at the same rate don't use up the fallback steps. */
+				link_train_max_retries++;
+				drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
+					   "retrying link training at rate=%d lanes=%d\n",
+					   ctrl->link->link_params.rate,
+					   ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes);
+			} else {
+				drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status(ctrl->aux, link_status);
 
-			if (!drm_dp_clock_recovery_ok(link_status,
-					ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes))
-				rc = msm_dp_ctrl_link_rate_down_shift(ctrl);
-			else
-				rc = msm_dp_ctrl_link_lane_down_shift(ctrl, panel);
+				if (!drm_dp_clock_recovery_ok(link_status,
+							      ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes))
+					rc = msm_dp_ctrl_link_rate_down_shift(ctrl);
+				else
+					rc = msm_dp_ctrl_link_lane_down_shift(ctrl, panel);
 
-			if (rc < 0) {
-				/* end with failure */
-				break; /* lane == 1 already */
+				if (rc < 0) {
+					/* end with failure */
+					break; /* lane == 1 already */
+				}
 			}
 
 			/* stop link training before start re training  */
-- 
